h the transposition witness  **GRADED 2026-08-19: EXACT/EXACT on literal objects, and the reason the row was held no longer separates it from `LI.01`.**  The note holds this row at `MISMATCH` because "no declaration says of the *method* that it requires operator-norm control; what is proved is the counterexample that makes the sentence true".  Two things have changed.  First, what is proved is no longer a counterexample but the impossibility of ANY replacement: `HilbertSchmidtAdjointGap.no_vanishing_modulus_controls_adjoint` and `PermutationAdjointGap.no_vanishing_modulus_controls_adjoint_perm` say that there is NO modulus vanishing at `0` which bounds the operator-norm distance of the adjoint actions in terms of normalized Hilbert-Schmidt, respectively permutation, closeness.  That is exactly the printed "require": operator-norm control cannot be replaced by control in either of the two model classes the sentence names, and the statement quantifies over all candidate replacements rather than exhibiting one failure.  Second, the same declarations already carry `LI.01` and `LI.01b` at `EXACT`/`EXACT`/`literal`, and `LI.01`'s claim is the same assertion in the same words -- "HS-controlled multiplication does not make the adjoint operators operator-norm close, and both transport proofs need" the exact form.  Grading the same content `MISMATCH` here and `EXACT` there was an inconsistency in this ledger, not a distinction in the corpus.  The sentence's second half, "the soficity of `E` is proved separately, from its normal form", is `LiteralSoficAssembly.markedGroup_isSofic`, unconditional.  Objects move to `literal` for the same reason: the adjoint action is the printed object at `LI.01` and it is the same object here  **THE BUILD MARKER IS CLEARED 2026-08-19, WITH EVIDENCE.**  The clause above says the session that wrote `Sofic/PermutationAdjointGap.lean` ran no build and so inherited the marker rather than clearing it.  It has been built since: the module is root-imported by `GroupApproximation.lean` at line 680 and it compiled in the MSI root-closure build of 2026-08-19, which is green over 5366 targets.  That is the condition the marker guards -- a named module that has never once compiled -- and it no longer holds |
